  "style": {
    "id": "murmuration",
    "name": "Murmuration",
    "description": "A dusk sky (warm horizon, cool zenith, low sun glow, a thin dark tree line with pylons for scale) where thousands of tiny near-black birds wheel as one living cloud. Nothing is placed: each bird has a closed-form position at time t — a blend between its point in the previous and next formation (seeded volumetric samples of a blob, a ribbon, an arrow, a ring, glyphs or an icon), plus a smooth 3D noise flow so the flock swirls and breathes, plus travelling density waves that bunch the birds and bank them toward the camera so a dark band rolls through the cloud. Edges stay soft with stragglers; the whole flock sways and turns as a body. Birds are two-triangle silhouettes that flap with a per-bird phase and point along their velocity (finite difference of the same closed form). The sound is a wing-rush whose level follows flock speed, a low whoosh per density wave, sparse distant calls and a gentle pad.",
